# Android database compatibility

The Android app was built first and depends on the existing AdvisorTrack database. Existing production tables and structures must remain backward-compatible.

Migration 026 is the accepted pattern: add a new linked table (`company_subscriptions`) without modifying Android-dependent structures.

## Allowed

- Additive database changes
- New tables
- New columns on existing tables only when they are demonstrably non-breaking and backward-compatible

## Not allowed

- Dropping existing tables or columns
- Renaming existing tables or columns
- Changing existing column data types
- Changing the existing meaning of a field
- Changing existing nullability/default semantics in a way that could affect Android
- Removing or repurposing existing constraints
- Altering existing relationships relied on by Android
- Restructuring existing core tables because a cleaner web-dashboard design is preferred

## If data cannot safely fit the existing schema

Prefer a new linked table. Do not reshape Android-dependent tables to suit the web dashboard.

## Stop condition

If a proposed change to an existing structure could affect Android behaviour, STOP and report it before implementing.
